add([(1810,'figure','Separate ROBROOT, WORLD, BASE and TOOL triads.')],'robroot','Robot root versus workpiece base','The diagram labels ROBROOT and BASE separately. What distinction should be retained?', [('Robot-root geometry and a chosen workpiece Base may be related by a nonidentity transform.','Distinct origins/axes in the figure do not imply that every workpiece frame equals the robot root.'),('ROBROOT and BASE must contain identical numbers because both are near the robot.','Physical proximity does not establish identical coordinate frames.'),('BASE is a joint-angle vector while ROBROOT is a colour image.','Both labels denote spatial frames here.'),('ROBROOT is the mobile TCP while BASE is the tool flange.','The figure labels TOOL separately; root and workpiece frames are not these tool frames.')],typ='diagram')
